 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508105,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You are awarded a $500 scholarship! In addition to the $1,500 you have saved for tuition, you now have an additional $500 to spend on credit hours for fall semester. Now, how many credit hours could you take this fall semester? Assume the cost is still $113 per credit hour.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Break the words into components. \n</p><table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>The number of credit hours you can take</td>\n<td>is no more than</td>\n<td>$1,500 saved</td>\n<td>plus</td>\n<td>$500 scholarship</td>\n<td>divided by</td>\n<td>$113 cost of one credit hour</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><i>H</i></td>\n<td>≤</td>\n<td>(1,500</td>\n<td>+</td>\n<td>500)</td>\n<td>/</td>\n<td>113</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>You can spend no more than the money you saved plus your scholarship.</p>\n<p>Solve <span data-math=\"H \\le \\frac{{1,500 + 500}}{{113}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"H \\le \\frac{{2,000}}{{113}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"H \\le 17.699....\"></span></p>\n<p>Since you can only take a whole number of credit hours, you can take at most 17 credit hours.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "You could take up to 17 credit hours and stay under $2,000."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
